# Force LF in the working tree for every text file.
#
# Many contract tests assert against source files using multi-line string
# literals that embed "\n", or locate a region by slicing between two
# multi-line boundary markers. On a Windows checkout with core.autocrlf=true
# those sources materialize CRLF, the literals cannot match, and
# `npm run test:contracts` fails on completely correct code.
#
# That is why the suite can pass in a long-lived working copy and fail in a
# newly created worktree or a fresh clone off the very same commit. Observed
# while validating the DSP delivery merge: sway-fee-policy failed on a fresh
# checkout and passed after normalizing to LF, with fee-policy.ts
# byte-identical between the two.
#
# Scope: this affects checkouts where core.autocrlf converts on checkout --
# in practice Windows. The current CI job runs on ubuntu-latest, where files
# are already LF, so this is not what makes CI red. It does protect any
# Windows runner or contributor, and it makes local results match CI.
#
# 3e61b27 fixed this for scripts/sway-seed-performer-previews.mjs by pinning
# that one file. The pin was never extended, and the same fragility has since
# reappeared in at least sway-fee-policy, sway-universal-account-pro-mode,
# sway-active-room-registry, and sway-event-ticket-native-ga. Enumerating
# affected files does not hold -- every new contract test that matches a
# multi-line literal reintroduces the bug. Pin globally instead.
#
# `text=auto` lets git detect binary files, so .png/.jpg are left alone.
# There are no .bat/.cmd files in this repo that would require CRLF.
* text=auto eol=lf
